  [gate 23p] the good split and all-fabric images and 1 bound-bitstream control pass the identity gate; 13 planted images each fail it by their kind (ddr3, ident, manifest, placement from the SoC; firmware, bitstream, placement and manifest from the image's files) in 30 s
test_every_recipe_elaborates:
  [gate 23g] 6/6 shipped recipes reach Instance("milan_datapath") in 11 s, each with the flow tail its own launcher appends (--build included, the flag every shape gate excludes). This proves a recipe RUNS, not that it builds the SoC its config describes - that comparison is gate 1e's and #155 carries where the two disagree
test_recipe_smoke_gate_bites:
  [gate 23g mutation] 2/2 recipes stripped of --entity-gen-dir refused to elaborate, which is #156 item 1 replayed on the recipes that shipped it
test_firmware_version_derived_from_rtl:
  [gate 24] firmware_version DERIVED from milan_csr VERSION 0x0002_0060 -> '2.96.0' all-fabric, '3.96.0' split: 5/5 configs derive it at their placement and declare none, it lands zero-padded at ENTITY+116 in all 5 ROMs (1722.1 7.2.1 Table 7-2), no entity_model_id moves with it or with the placement (6.2.2.8 exclusion; arty_current still pinned 0x001BC50AC1000006), firmware_rev 7 -> 2.96.7 with the same id, 4/4 bad declarations refused
